<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Prato</h1><p class="st-meta">1140 CE – 1351 CE (approx.) · capital Prato</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Tuscan wool-making city-republic, home of the merchant Francesco Datini, which was sold to Florence in 1351.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Prato grew around the castle of the Alberti counts and the parish church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prato-cathedral">Santo Stefano</a>, and consuls governed it by 1140. The commune developed in the shadow of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-florence">Florence</a>, a few miles away.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Prato was ruled by consuls and later a podestà, and its economy rested on wool cloth production, using the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bisenzio">Bisenzio</a> river to power fulling mills. The cathedral holds the relic of the Virgin's girdle, a major object of devotion. From the early 14th century the town placed itself under the Angevin kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> to keep its independence from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-florence">Florence</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1351 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joanna-i-of-naples">Queen Joanna I of Naples</a> sold her rights over Prato to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-florence">Republic of Florence</a>, which ruled it from then on. The merchant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-di-marco-datini">Francesco Datini</a>, born there around 1335, made his fortune in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> before returning to Prato, where his huge archive survives.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1140 CE – 1351 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.39%;width:4.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1140 CE – 1351 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Prato</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tuscan Italian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Prato</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1246&amp;focus=commune-of-prato" aria-label="Commune of Prato on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4946 623 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Commune of Prato lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5266 879L5349 976M5266 879L5270 883"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5349 976h0M5270 883h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5266 879h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5266 879h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Prato. <a href="/atlas?year=1246&amp;focus=commune-of-prato">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
